 "text": "Hello! How' everything today? It' bit more than that. A typical century ride these days is about hundred and twenty to one hundred and fifty miles. If you average thirty miles an hour, you'd be on the horse for about four hours. With stops it' more like four and a half. It is. Plan on starting early and stopping for food and toilet breaks along the way. Nice approach. Ride few shorter rides first to build up your distance and endurance. Mix short and long rides, with a few easy days thrown in. Short rides build your base, long rides push your limits.",
